# 3.5 Carat Radiant Cut Diamond Ring: The $51K vs $6.7K Truth

A 3.5 carat radiant cut diamond ring sits at the edge of statement jewelry and genuine wealth. The face-up size is approximately 9.5×7.2mm — larger than a 3ct, undeniably present, the kind of stone that gets noticed before you extend your hand.

In current certified market inventory, lab 3.5ct radiant rings start at [$6,711](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Natural 3.5ct radiant rings start at [$51,841](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

That gap — 7.7× — is the widest in the entire radiant weight series. It is also the most important number in this guide.

At every other weight in the radiant series, the lab-to-natural gap narrows as carat weight drops. At 3.5ct, it widens — because GIA-certified natural radiant stones at this weight are genuinely scarce and priced accordingly.

**TL;DR:**
- → **The 7.7× Gap:** lab 3.5ct radiant ring at [$6,711](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), natural entry at [$51,841](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — the widest lab-to-natural gap in the radiant series
- → **Best lab pick:** [3.50ct D-VVS1 IGI $5,851](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$6,711](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — D-VVS1 IGI, 9.5mm face-up
- → **Natural entry:** [3.52ct F-VS1 GIA $50,981](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$51,841](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — GIA certified, F-VS1
- → **Natural sweet spot:** [3.51ct D-VVS1 GIA $52,754](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24468417?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [$860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$53,614](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24468417?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — top color and clarity at this weight
- 3.5ct radiant face-up: ~9.5×7.2mm. Crosses [The 9.5mm Statement](#the-9-5mm-statement) threshold — visible across a room in any light
- The half-carat upgrade from 3ct costs $9,029 more in natural. [The Half-Carat Premium](#the-half-carat-premium) explains why that number is higher per carat than the base stone
- See the [radiant cut engagement rings pillar](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) for the full shape guide

