## The Half-Carat Premium

The Half-Carat Premium is the price acceleration that happens between 3ct and 3.5ct in natural radiant diamonds. It is not linear.

At 3ct, the natural radiant entry is [$41,952](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28034285?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for the stone — approximately [$13,100 per carat](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=2.9-3.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). At 3.5ct, the natural entry is [$50,981](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — approximately [$14,484 per carat](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=3.4-3.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). That is a [$9,029](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) jump for half a carat more.

The math matters. You are paying roughly [$18,000 per carat](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=3.4-3.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for the incremental 0.5ct — not [$14,000](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=2.9-3.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). This is the Half-Carat Premium at work.

For natural buyers, this premium reflects genuine scarcity. Fewer 3.5ct natural radiant stones exist in certified inventory than at 3ct. The market prices rarity accordingly.

If you want 3.5ct natural, that premium is unavoidable. It is not a retailer margin — it is the cost of a rare stone at a rare weight.

For lab buyers, the Half-Carat Premium barely registers. Lab at 3ct was [$6,210](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929424?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Lab at 3.5ct is [$6,711](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

The extra half carat costs just [$501](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). That is the full cost of [The Half-Carat Premium](#the-half-carat-premium) for lab buyers — less than most setting upgrades.

Lab is not subject to natural scarcity premiums. At 3.5ct, that difference becomes the clearest argument in the entire series for choosing lab over natural.

