> **Farzana on Lab 3.5ct:**
>
> The D-VVS1 IGI at [$6,711](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) complete is almost unfair. For [$501 more](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) than the 3ct lab ring, you gain half a carat and cross the [9.5mm threshold](#the-9-5mm-statement). No other upgrade in this series delivers that much face-up presence for so little extra spend.
>
> The IF and FL grades at [$10,794](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27423134?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) are for buyers who need the certificate to say a specific thing. Not for buyers who want a more beautiful stone — because at 3.5ct radiant, VVS1 is already eye-clean with room to spare.

