## Expert Summary

A 3.5 carat radiant cut diamond ring crosses [The 9.5mm Statement](#the-9-5mm-statement) — the face-up size where a radiant becomes visible from across a room. Both lab and natural stones deliver this presence at 3.5ct. The decision between them is not about quality — it is about origin, rarity, and how far your budget stretches.

Lab at [$6,711](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) complete is the best face-up-per-dollar in the entire [radiant cut engagement rings](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) series. The half-carat upgrade from 3ct costs just [$501](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28472159?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in lab — always take it.

Natural at [$51,841](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) entry is subject to [The Half-Carat Premium](#the-half-carat-premium) — you pay roughly [$18,000 per carat](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28049659?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for the incremental weight above 3ct. The [D-VVS1 GIA at $53,614](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24468417?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the strongest natural pick at this weight. The 7.7× lab-to-natural gap is the widest in the series — and that gap only grows as carat weight increases.

This data is sourced from certified market inventory as of {{month_year}}. Prices change — verify current pricing before purchase.

